; The zone the proxy scenarios are asked about - slice P4c, feeding P8.
;
; WHY A ZONE OF ITS OWN RATHER THAN MORE NAMES IN ok.test. Every name in ok.test
; resolves into a documentation range on purpose, so that a run against the DNS
; bench cannot open a connection to anything. These names have to do the
; opposite: a proxy scenario is only worth anything if a real request can be sent
; and then found again in somebody's log. Keeping the two apart means the rule
; stated in ok.test.zone stays true rather than acquiring exceptions.
;
; THE THREE SCENARIO NAMES POINT AT ONE AND THE SAME SERVER, AND THAT IS THE
; WHOLE EXPERIMENTAL DESIGN. via, direct and auth are the same address, the same
; port and the same content. The only thing that differs between them is what the
; PAC file says about them. So when one request turns up in the proxy log and
; another does not, the PAC is the only thing that can have caused it - there is
; no second variable to blame.
;
; Every address is inside the bench's own subnet and unreachable from anywhere
; else, the same deliberate exception partner.test already documents.
$ORIGIN proxy.test.
$TTL 60

@   IN SOA ns.proxy.test. admin.proxy.test. (
        1          ; serial
        7200       ; refresh
        3600       ; retry
        1209600    ; expire
        3600 )     ; minimum

@   IN NS  ns.proxy.test.
ns  IN A   172.28.0.53

; The server that hands out the PAC file over plain HTTP, which is how a machine
; normally gets one. It is also the origin the three names below answer from.
pac     IN A   172.28.0.90

; The proxy itself. It is named here because a PAC file naming a bare address is
; a PAC file nobody would recognise, and because the name is what a person reads
; in a report.
gw      IN A   172.28.0.128

; PAC says: go through the open proxy. This request MUST appear in the proxy log.
via     IN A   172.28.0.90

; PAC says: go direct, even though a proxy is configured. This request MUST NOT
; appear in the proxy log - the negative half of the oracle, and the half that
; gives the positive one its meaning.
direct  IN A   172.28.0.90

; PAC says: go through the proxy that demands credentials. Reaching it without
; any produces 407, which is the fact P8-K3 has to detect.
auth    IN A   172.28.0.90
